+/*
+ * PUCK BRIDGE'S LIST STYLES (pb 5, owner 2026-10-14: "all three, able to change it in settings"). The panes list and
+ * the tabs, drawn one of three ways over the same carousel (its position, momentum and settling are the classic
+ * pages'): CARDS, a column of cards scrolled up and down, the middle one large with a green rim; DIAL, the clock's
+ * ring with a segment per row, the chosen one long, and its name large in the middle, turned sideways; COMPACT, five
+ * rows under a fixed green band, scrolled up and down. Every row says what it is doing: orange "Working · 1:23", white
+ * "Reply ready", else "Idle"; a tab, how many chats or sessions it holds and how many work. A tap on any row opens it
+ * (a tab: switches to it); browsing switches nothing.
